## F1 (finding)

- target: segment:scope-adaptive-system

- at: 7b429bcc

The $\pi_0$ rule ("the law of the world given what the agent knows by design") is a conditional probability with no named base measure or class of possible worlds, while a physical world has one law. The rule then leaves three cases undecided: a filter built with a wrong model (whether it is in depends on the unnamed class); a hard-coded true guess (knowledge or belief?); a pretrained design. Candidate completion, untested: $\pi_0$ is a declared base measure over a declared class, conditioned on the evidence the design process had and built in, not on its conclusions. With (h′) only the support matters. 07 §2.3.

## F2 (finding)

